## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design traffic shaping at the CNF data plane, considering multi-tenant isolation and simple orchestration.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant traffic prioritization
- Sidecar data-plane logic with header-based decisions
- Lightweight state via Redis and a simple token bucket
- Minimal manifests to validate end-to-end

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo in-sidecar router
function route(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['X-TENANT-ID'];
  const pri = req.headers['X-TENANT-PRIORITY'] || 'normal';
  const pathHash = hash(req.path);
  if(pri === 'high') return forwardFast(req);
  const key = `tenant:${tenant}:path:${pathHash}`;
  if(redis.incr(key) > RATE_LIMIT){
    return reject(429, 'Too many requests');
  }
  redis.pexpire(key, 60000);
  return forwardSlow(req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this with a canary tenant without affecting others?
- What monitoring would you add to ensure fairness during bursts?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design cross-tenant observability with strict data isolation, covering tracing, logging, sampling, and validation.

## Key Concepts

- OpenTelemetry and trace propagation
- Tenant isolation and boundary enforcement
- Per-tenant sampling and data redaction
- Validation in a single-namespace scenario

## Code Example

```javascript
// PII redaction example (logs)
function redactLogEvent(event, tenantId) {
  const safe = {...event};
  if (safe.message) safe.message = safe.message.replace(/\b(email|ssn|password)\b[^:]*: [^,]+/gi, 'PII_REDACTED');
  if (safe.user && safe.user.id) safe.user.id = 'REDACTED';
  return safe;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and remediate cross-tenant leakage in traces?
- What metrics would you surface to confirm per-tenant isolation is preserved during incidents?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design comprehensive runtime security controls for cloud-native network functions, focusing on continuous compliance verification and automated remediation beyond static image signing.

## Key Concepts
- Runtime attestation and drift detection
- SBOM-based compliance validation
- Tenant-isolated cryptographic identity
- Mutual TLS for secure communication
- Policy enforcement with OPA/Kyverno
- Automated rollback and recovery mechanisms

